WEBVTT

00:05.540 --> 00:07.710
<b>MIZUHO</b>

00:05.540 --> 00:07.710
<b>TEMPLE</b>

02:00.790 --> 02:02.960
Welcome back, Tsuchiura.

02:02.960 --> 02:04.630
How did it go?

02:04.630 --> 02:06.380
My apologies, Master.

02:06.380 --> 02:09.380
I'm afraid that Naotsugu Miura
escaped from me.

02:09.670 --> 02:11.580
There is no excuse for my failure.

02:11.580 --> 02:14.670
I will accept whatever punishment
you deem fit.

02:15.790 --> 02:20.880
Come now, Tsuchiura.
I have never doubted your loyalty to me.

02:20.880 --> 02:23.960
A single failed mission
does nothing to shake that faith.

02:23.960 --> 02:27.790
Just make up for it
when the next opportunity arises.

02:27.790 --> 02:30.040
Yessir. Thank you very much.

02:30.040 --> 02:32.130
Naotsugu Miura
won't escape alive next time.

02:32.130 --> 02:33.790
You can forget about him.

02:33.790 --> 02:37.170
I need you to go to Kyoto instead.

02:37.460 --> 02:38.790
Kyoto?

02:39.130 --> 02:41.380
The situation there is tumultuous.

02:41.380 --> 02:43.670
My lord has been using the Shinsengumi

02:43.670 --> 02:46.750
to police Kyoto and
keep the imperialist at bay,

02:46.750 --> 02:48.830
but the tides are shifting against them.

02:48.830 --> 02:51.000
And that's where you come in.

02:51.580 --> 02:54.420
I've already sent about
100 demons to Kyoto.

02:51.580 --> 02:56.170
WOVEN BY A SINGLE THREAD

02:54.420 --> 02:56.210
They are only lesser demons,

02:56.210 --> 02:59.920
but I want you to take command of them
to strike down the enemy.

03:00.420 --> 03:01.420
Yessir.

03:01.420 --> 03:04.960
But if I may, how did you get
100 demons on your side?

03:04.960 --> 03:08.710
Easily enough.
Thanks to a certain mystical sake.

03:08.710 --> 03:13.040
Although, it's become impossible
to obtain now.

03:15.580 --> 03:17.540
Understood.

03:21.750 --> 03:25.420
Master Yasuhide.
May I ask you just one thing?

03:25.420 --> 03:26.830
Go ahead.

03:27.330 --> 03:30.710
Why was it necessary for me to attack
Naotsugu Miura in front of that man

03:30.710 --> 03:34.040
at the cost of exposing my true form?

03:34.290 --> 03:36.460
Because necessity demanded it.

03:36.460 --> 03:39.040
Or is that answer
not satisfying enough for you?

03:39.630 --> 03:40.540
No, sir.

03:40.540 --> 03:42.920
Then go fulfill your duty, Tsuchiura.

03:42.920 --> 03:44.040
Yessir.

03:45.290 --> 03:49.080
I will see to it that everyone who stands
against you is dead and buried, Master.

04:09.330 --> 04:11.000
Look! It's the demon kid!

04:11.000 --> 04:12.080
Stop that!

04:12.080 --> 04:14.000
You don't know what he'll do
if you get too close!

04:14.000 --> 04:16.250
Neener, neener! Freaky creature!

04:16.250 --> 04:19.000
Enough! Do as I say, young man!

04:19.000 --> 04:20.040
Now let's go!

04:20.040 --> 04:21.750
But, Mom, just look at him!

04:21.750 --> 04:24.250
No more! You're going to worry me sick!

04:51.750 --> 04:53.080
Nomari...

04:56.960 --> 04:59.540
Yet another thing I've lost.

05:06.790 --> 05:08.920
Winter daphnes?

05:13.500 --> 05:15.170
I've been looking all over.

05:15.170 --> 05:17.210
You just vanished without a word.

05:20.630 --> 05:22.960
So, this is where you've been?

05:23.460 --> 05:25.960
I'm surprised you knew where to find me.

05:26.250 --> 05:28.290
I had no idea, actually.

05:28.290 --> 05:33.540
I just went around to every place
that I imagined you might go.

05:38.290 --> 05:39.880
Are you okay?

05:40.380 --> 05:43.330
I'm not flimsy enough
to die from a few hits.

05:43.330 --> 05:45.130
That's not what I meant.

05:50.920 --> 05:53.170
What are you going to do now?

05:53.170 --> 05:56.580
Kill Tsuchiura. The demon from earlier.

05:57.670 --> 05:59.130
That's absurd.

05:59.130 --> 06:03.750
You couldn't even leave a mark on him
when you two fought, remember?

06:03.750 --> 06:08.670
Even so, I can't afford to back down
in pursuit of my goal.

06:10.670 --> 06:12.080
Jinya-kun...

06:13.290 --> 06:15.500
I've always wanted to ask.

06:15.500 --> 06:18.420
Why are you so driven to fight demons?

06:22.540 --> 06:25.670
It all goes back twenty some years ago...

06:26.290 --> 06:29.960
when I lived in a blacksmithing village
known as Kadono.

06:30.290 --> 06:35.080
I had no talent for forging swords,
but I was good at wielding them.

06:35.630 --> 06:38.880
So I was assigned
to guard the village shrine maiden.

06:39.500 --> 06:41.460
Her name was Byakuya.

06:42.330 --> 06:45.210
You loved her, I'm guessing?

06:46.000 --> 06:47.130
Yeah.

06:47.920 --> 06:51.830
She gave up her own happiness
for the sake of Kadono.

06:51.830 --> 06:53.380
And became the shrine maiden.

06:54.080 --> 06:56.330
Her actions struck a chord with me,

06:56.330 --> 06:58.920
so I wished for nothing
other than to keep her safe.

07:01.330 --> 07:05.210
Until one day,
Kadono came under attack by demons.

07:05.210 --> 07:08.080
Even though I was supposed
to be her sentinel,

07:08.670 --> 07:11.000
I couldn't save her from death.

07:11.000 --> 07:13.290
That was the day I lost everything.

07:14.080 --> 07:16.130
It left me full of rage.

07:16.130 --> 07:18.460
I hated the demon who did it.

07:19.170 --> 07:21.000
A century from now,

07:21.000 --> 07:24.420
that same one is destined to become
an evil deity who rules over demonkind

07:24.420 --> 07:28.210
and will return to Kadono
before laying waste to the world.

07:29.130 --> 07:31.040
I must stop that demon god.

07:31.040 --> 07:33.460
It's the sole reason for my existence.

07:34.250 --> 07:38.790
That's why I hunted demons
to consume them and steal their power.

07:39.460 --> 07:41.880
I wanted to become
a force to be reckoned with.

07:42.880 --> 07:45.960
The name of the demon
who killed Byakuya is Suzune.

07:46.670 --> 07:48.580
She's my little sister.

07:50.420 --> 07:57.380
So, you're saying the reason you wanted
so much power was to kill your own sister?

07:57.580 --> 07:59.000
Who knows.

08:00.420 --> 08:02.710
You're not going to answer me, huh?

08:03.130 --> 08:04.580
I'm sorry.

08:04.580 --> 08:06.420
I'm not trying to deflect.

08:06.420 --> 08:09.000
I honestly don't know what to say.

08:09.000 --> 08:12.290
Then let me ask you a different question.

08:12.460 --> 08:14.920
I understand you fight to gain power.

08:14.920 --> 08:18.290
As part of the larger goal
of stopping your sister.

08:18.670 --> 08:22.790
But why exactly do you
feel the need to stop Suzune?

08:23.290 --> 08:26.290
You might be forced to kill her.

08:26.290 --> 08:28.880
And I can't understand
why you would choose

08:28.880 --> 08:30.920
to follow this path in spite of that.

08:30.920 --> 08:31.830
Well, I...

08:32.040 --> 08:35.000
Are you fighting to protect other people?

08:35.000 --> 08:36.880
Or to satisfy your hatred?

08:36.880 --> 08:40.040
Is it revenge that
you ultimately want from all this?

08:40.960 --> 08:42.170
No.

08:42.500 --> 08:45.920
I'm not doing it for
righteousness or revenge.

08:46.380 --> 08:50.080
Even now, Suzune holds
a very special place in my heart.

08:50.080 --> 08:52.880
But the rage won't let me go.

08:52.880 --> 08:57.710
I'm still consumed by hatred for her,
enough to make me bloodthirsty.

08:57.710 --> 09:01.380
Yet at the same time,
a part of me hesitates to kill her.

09:01.380 --> 09:04.790
Despite all the decades
that I've been alive,

09:04.790 --> 09:07.170
I can't even figure out
what my heart truly want from me.

09:09.460 --> 09:12.210
But I swore to stop her, regardless.

09:12.210 --> 09:13.830
And I'm certain

09:13.830 --> 09:17.170
that desire didn't come from a
savior complex or my hatred of Suzune.

09:17.170 --> 09:22.000
I merely wanted to put a satisfying period
on my way of life.

09:22.790 --> 09:25.380
What I truly wanted to kill...

09:25.380 --> 09:27.540
was that flawed part of me.

09:29.540 --> 09:32.000
I'm so pathetic.

09:32.880 --> 09:36.290
The reality is while I wanted to kill her
from hatred on one hand,

09:36.290 --> 09:39.330
I wanted save her
through forgiveness on the other.

09:39.330 --> 09:41.210
But in the end,

09:41.210 --> 09:45.290
those were just excuses I made
to avoid dealing with my own spinelessness.

09:46.420 --> 09:49.210
I can already tell this rage
will never subside

09:49.210 --> 09:51.830
and will lead me
to the worst possible outcome.

09:52.750 --> 09:55.790
My way of life was a mistake.

09:56.500 --> 09:57.920
I'm glad.

09:59.210 --> 10:03.710
You're still the same Jinya-kun
who I've always known.

10:03.710 --> 10:07.000
You're a good person
who can admit when they're wrong.

10:07.670 --> 10:11.460
But tell me, is being in the right
really so important?

10:11.460 --> 10:12.960
Remember my dad?

10:12.960 --> 10:16.500
He literally abandoned
everything he had just for me.

10:17.170 --> 10:19.330
Looking back at it now,

10:19.330 --> 10:23.880
I think that was the wrong choice
for any normal person to make.

10:23.880 --> 10:25.250
But it's because...

10:25.250 --> 10:26.460
No.

10:26.460 --> 10:30.460
It doesn't matter what his reasons were.
They don't justify his choice.

10:30.460 --> 10:33.920
Since there are still people out there
who suffered as a result.

10:36.670 --> 10:39.670
Still, he did save me.

10:39.920 --> 10:42.750
You have to realize that
doing the right thing in the right way

10:42.750 --> 10:45.580
doesn't always lead to a perfect outcome.

10:46.210 --> 10:47.790
At the very least,

10:47.790 --> 10:52.330
I'm able to be here today
because that's where his mistake led me.

10:55.000 --> 10:57.670
Waging a war to kill your sister.

10:57.670 --> 11:00.290
Consuming demons for their power.

11:00.290 --> 11:02.580
You do all of that in service to yourself.

11:02.920 --> 11:04.830
So, you're right.

11:04.830 --> 11:08.170
The path you've taken
and the events that put you on it,

11:08.170 --> 11:10.040
those were all mistakes.

11:10.880 --> 11:15.080
But even so, there are people
who were saved by your actions.

11:18.130 --> 11:19.630
Why are you here?

11:20.210 --> 11:21.460
Please forgive me.

11:21.460 --> 11:24.000
We've been eavesdropping for awhile now.

11:25.170 --> 11:29.880
Miura-sama has been helping me
look for you with Nomari-chan.

11:30.250 --> 11:32.080
Because he wanted to apologize.

11:33.170 --> 11:34.920
I'll be frank.

11:34.920 --> 11:37.460
Your demonic form terrifies me.

11:37.460 --> 11:40.540
The fear of facing something drastically
more powerful than any mere man

11:40.540 --> 11:42.630
caused me to run away.

11:44.670 --> 11:47.750
As you can see, I'm a monster.

11:47.750 --> 11:50.000
It's not wrong for you to feel that way.

11:50.000 --> 11:51.040
No!

11:51.330 --> 11:53.670
I've seen you agonize
over doing what is right,

11:53.670 --> 11:58.880
yet still brave mortal danger
to stay true to your path in life.

11:58.880 --> 12:01.250
You and I are the same in that respect.

12:01.750 --> 12:06.710
Although you may be a demon,
you have never been a monster!

12:07.250 --> 12:08.540
Jin-dono!

12:08.540 --> 12:10.750
You are my good friend.

12:11.630 --> 12:14.040
I know I ran away once.

12:14.040 --> 12:16.420
But I never want to do it again.

12:16.630 --> 12:18.420
I would like...

12:18.420 --> 12:20.790
to stay your friend until the very end!

12:24.630 --> 12:26.000
Daddy!

12:36.540 --> 12:38.000
Nomari...

12:38.000 --> 12:40.000
don't I scare you?

12:41.000 --> 12:44.330
I'm not scared!
Because you're my daddy!

12:44.330 --> 12:47.920
So please don't disappear again!

12:56.000 --> 12:58.580
Always the doting dad, aren't you?

12:58.580 --> 12:59.920
That's for sure.

12:59.920 --> 13:03.880
All it takes is the word "daddy"
for him to go all soft and schmaltzy.

13:14.920 --> 13:18.290
This little scene is what
all your mistakes gave birth to.

13:18.290 --> 13:21.420
See? Not so bad after all, is it?

13:22.540 --> 13:24.880
Yeah, you're right.

13:26.000 --> 13:27.830
It really is.

13:34.250 --> 13:35.670
I'll admit it.

13:35.920 --> 13:39.330
Justifying everything about myself
with hatred as an excuse...

13:39.330 --> 13:42.880
that lifestyle was a mistake
from the beginning.

13:43.080 --> 13:44.290
However,

13:44.290 --> 13:47.960
accepting that won't change the fact
the demon god is coming in the future.

13:48.580 --> 13:51.420
In all likelihood,
hatred will continue to consume me

13:51.420 --> 13:53.920
until Suzune and I face off
in a battle to the death.

13:54.380 --> 13:55.630
Considering that...

13:56.380 --> 13:58.420
is it truly all right for me

13:58.420 --> 14:01.420
to reach out with this hand once more
and dream of being a guardian?

14:01.630 --> 14:05.670
You've already kept many people
and things safe from harm.

14:05.670 --> 14:08.670
You just refused to believe it.

14:09.790 --> 14:11.130
I see.

14:18.420 --> 14:20.330
Well, I should get going.

14:23.080 --> 14:24.380
I'm sorry.

14:25.170 --> 14:27.210
I always have to rely on you in the end.

14:28.080 --> 14:29.670
Don't worry about it.

14:29.670 --> 14:31.500
Fight fire with fire, as they say.

14:31.500 --> 14:33.710
Best to let a demon to hunt the demons.

14:33.710 --> 14:35.000
Please forgive-

14:35.000 --> 14:36.130
Never mind.

14:36.130 --> 14:37.880
Thank you!

14:38.130 --> 14:40.670
I am going to fulfill my purpose.

14:40.670 --> 14:42.080
You should do the same.

14:42.080 --> 14:45.040
Uphold your duty both as a human
and a samurai.

14:45.420 --> 14:46.630
Daddy!

14:46.880 --> 14:48.210
Daddy!

14:50.960 --> 14:52.040
Ofuu.

14:52.040 --> 14:53.750
Watch after Nomari for me.

14:56.170 --> 14:59.080
You're not going
to disappear again, right?

14:59.080 --> 15:00.460
Yeah.

15:00.460 --> 15:02.750
No more playing hide and seek.

15:02.750 --> 15:04.960
So be a good girl and wait for me, okay?

15:04.960 --> 15:07.290
'Kay, Daddy!

15:13.880 --> 15:17.880
Good luck! Please come back safe!

15:18.170 --> 15:19.670
We'll be waiting!

15:27.290 --> 15:29.790
Yo, Tsuchiura! Glad you made it.

15:34.210 --> 15:37.880
As taciturn as ever, I see.

15:41.540 --> 15:42.960
This is the second one.

15:42.960 --> 15:45.750
I played a little
with the temper pattern this time.

15:45.750 --> 15:48.080
I made it a mix of waves and streaks.

15:48.080 --> 15:51.630
It's stylish and sleek,
just like a fine woman.

15:52.500 --> 15:55.710
You better leave it at that, Kaneomi.

15:55.710 --> 15:57.710
You're making your pupil uncomfortable.

15:57.710 --> 16:00.500
Aw, come on, Yato! Just look at it!

16:00.500 --> 16:03.130
This is the sexiest blade I've made.

16:03.380 --> 16:06.710
And you wonder why
people call you a weirdo.

16:06.880 --> 16:09.080
What are you giving me the stink eye for?

16:09.080 --> 16:10.790
You're my wife, aren'tcha?

16:11.830 --> 16:13.830
Not you, too, buddy!

16:14.210 --> 16:15.750
Sorry, I didn't mean to...

16:20.710 --> 16:23.130
Oh! Your little lady friend is here.

16:23.130 --> 16:26.130
Yeesh.
Always gotta flaunt your stuff, don'tcha?

16:26.130 --> 16:27.250
All right.

16:27.250 --> 16:30.580
Guess you can head out a little early today,
once we finish cleaning up.

16:30.830 --> 16:31.920
But sir...

16:31.920 --> 16:33.540
You heard me.

16:33.880 --> 16:36.040
There's no need to feel bad.

16:36.040 --> 16:38.130
We could all use a break once in a while.

16:40.790 --> 16:42.250
All right.

16:42.250 --> 16:44.290
Then, if you insist...

16:44.630 --> 16:45.630
Great!

16:45.630 --> 16:47.580
But just one thing.

16:47.580 --> 16:50.670
Why do you always listen to what she says?

16:50.670 --> 16:52.830
I'm supposed to be in charge, y'know!

17:21.670 --> 17:23.130
Took you long enough.

17:23.130 --> 17:24.460
You again.

17:25.540 --> 17:27.130
I've been waiting.

17:32.290 --> 17:35.670
Not long ago, I had a little chat
with a group of demons.

17:35.670 --> 17:37.710
Seems you're heading for Kyoto, eh?

17:39.250 --> 17:41.040
You defeated them?

17:41.040 --> 17:44.040
It took longer than expected,
but they made for a good warm up.

17:44.790 --> 17:46.250
Why?

17:46.250 --> 17:50.790
Why would you kill your own brethren
just to get in the way of Master Yasuhide?

17:51.000 --> 17:53.290
Now that you've been
publicly exposed as a demon,

17:53.290 --> 17:56.250
you should have no reason to fight
on behalf of the humans.

17:56.250 --> 17:58.790
I don't understand your objective.

17:59.420 --> 18:01.420
Ideology isn't my thing.

18:01.420 --> 18:04.290
Kick the foreigners out or don't.
It matters little to me.

18:05.250 --> 18:07.540
At least, that's what I thought...

18:08.380 --> 18:14.130
but it turns out that I really hate how
Yasuhide Hatakeyama conducts his business.

18:17.000 --> 18:19.920
The strife happening in Kyoto
is between humans.

18:19.920 --> 18:22.040
They're fighting to decide
this country's future.

18:22.040 --> 18:25.670
We monsters have no place in that.

18:25.670 --> 18:27.630
And that's why you're doing this?

18:27.630 --> 18:28.670
No.

18:28.960 --> 18:31.420
I'm not that much of a whimsical meddler.

18:31.420 --> 18:33.670
My reason is far more simple.

18:34.290 --> 18:36.630
I have a friend
on the battlefield of Kyoto.

18:36.630 --> 18:38.420
So I can't let you pass.

18:39.670 --> 18:41.290
Are you serious?

18:41.290 --> 18:44.170
I thought I had no right to take a stand.

18:44.830 --> 18:49.000
I'm a monster of hatred
out to kill his own sister, after all.

18:49.000 --> 18:52.250
The idea seemed so ridiculous
I couldn't even say it aloud.

18:53.290 --> 18:56.460
But someone helped me realize
there are lives that can be saved

18:56.460 --> 18:58.040
even in the face of my mistakes.

18:59.170 --> 19:00.250
So...

19:00.920 --> 19:05.130
I am going to stay the course
with a little show of grit.

19:05.130 --> 19:08.460
And in the name
of all that I wish to protect...

19:10.250 --> 19:13.000
I shall wield this blade once more!

19:13.580 --> 19:14.750
Very well.

19:30.920 --> 19:34.210
So, you have a set of tenets
that you believe in, too?

19:34.460 --> 19:35.380
Yeah.

19:35.380 --> 19:37.420
I'm not going to be the one
who backs down.

19:38.000 --> 19:39.670
Well, neither am I.

19:45.210 --> 19:45.670
I'll crush you!

19:45.670 --> 19:46.380
I'll crush you!

19:45.670 --> 19:46.380
I'll kill you!

20:10.630 --> 20:13.000
Try all you like, it's pointless!

20:13.000 --> 20:14.420
That's what you think.

20:14.420 --> 20:18.080
I know your power
can make your body harder than steel.

20:18.080 --> 20:22.040
But you sacrifice
all of your mobility while using it.

20:22.330 --> 20:23.830
And so what?

20:23.830 --> 20:28.170
Even if that's true, it doesn't change
the fact that you can't hurt me!

20:47.710 --> 20:49.790
Like I said, it's pointless.

20:56.250 --> 20:59.670
You have absolute confidence
in your indomitability,

20:59.670 --> 21:02.170
which is why you took my attack head on.

21:02.170 --> 21:06.500
Sure, I may not have any tricks
up my sleeve that can breach your defense.

21:06.500 --> 21:09.040
But luckily, I don't need to.

21:09.420 --> 21:12.580
Because I have the ability
to absorb your power instead!

21:15.920 --> 21:17.080
Assimilation.

21:31.920 --> 21:34.790
People are saying
the Imperial Regent passed away.

21:34.790 --> 21:38.250
So it seems like the reign
of Toyotomi is now at an end.

21:38.250 --> 21:40.170
The world will get violent again.

21:42.460 --> 21:46.000
Soon enough, I'm sure a war
will break out to shape the next era.

21:46.380 --> 21:48.630
Which means the smithery
will get busy, too.

21:53.080 --> 21:54.330
What's wrong?

21:55.710 --> 21:58.540
Nothing. I'm fine.

22:00.540 --> 22:03.290
I'm here to listen if you need
to get something off your chest.

22:04.710 --> 22:06.040
All right.

22:07.130 --> 22:09.330
Then, hear me out...
